# SABOTAGE: the fail-closed half of the aggregate — an UNEVALUABLE member. A verifier whose
# child produced no parseable report (a crash, a missing task, a compile error) must FAIL the
# fleet. Returning an empty violation list instead makes that member a normal `"ok"` document,
# so a tree the fleet could not fully evaluate reports a green aggregate — the exact
# "passing but proving nothing" outcome the runner_error path exists to refuse. The document
# still parses and the aggregate still folds, so only the test that injects an `{:error, _}`
# runner catches it.
# APP: samen_core
# TEST_FILES: test/verify_fleet_test.exs
# MUST_FAIL: an UNEVALUABLE member is a runner_error and fails the fleet
diff --git a/samen_core/lib/samen/verifier/fleet.ex b/samen_core/lib/samen/verifier/fleet.ex
--- a/samen_core/lib/samen/verifier/fleet.ex
+++ b/samen_core/lib/samen/verifier/fleet.ex
@@ -105,13 +105,8 @@
   reported violation and needs no special case.
   """
   @spec error_document(map(), String.t()) :: map()
-  def error_document(entry, reason) do
-    Samen.Verifier.document(entry.task, [
-      %{
-        kind: :runner_error,
-        message: "`mix #{entry.task}` could not be evaluated: #{reason}"
-      }
-    ])
+  def error_document(entry, _reason) do
+    Samen.Verifier.document(entry.task, [])
   end
 
   @doc """
